text: ["As Council of the Absolute enters the battlefield, choose a noncreature, nonland card name.\\nYour opponents can't cast spells with the chosen name.\\nSpells with the chosen name you cast cost {2} less to cast.", "At the beginning of each combat, up to one target creature attacks or blocks this combat if able and up to one target creature can't attack or block this combat.", 'At the beginning of each end step, each player discards their hand.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, return a creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Attacking creatures you control get +1/+0 and have menace.', 'Azorius Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Battalion — Whenever Boros Mastiff and at least two other creatures attack, Boros Mastiff gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Bloodrush — {1}{R}, Discard Pyrewild Shaman: Target attacking creature gets +3/+1 until end of turn.\\nWhenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, if Pyrewild Shaman is in your graveyard, you may pay {3}. If you do, return Pyrewild Shaman to your hand.', 'Bloodrush — {R}, Discard Rubblebelt Maaka: Target attacking creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Boros Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Change the text of target permanent by replacing all instances of one color word with another or one basic land type with another until end of turn.\\nCipher (Then you may exile this spell card encoded on a creature you control. Whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player, its controller may cast a copy of the encoded card without paying its mana cost.)', "Choose any target. Draw three cards, then discard a card. Blast of Genius deals damage equal to the discarded card's mana value to that permanent or player.", 'Choose target creature. Mill four cards, then that creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn for each land card in your graveyard.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {6}.', "Counter target spell. At the beginning of your next precombat main phase, add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is that spell's mana value.", "Counter target spell. Its controller can't cast spells this turn.", 'Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Create a 5/5 green Wurm creature token with trample.', 'Creatures you control gain indestructible until end of turn. Untap each creature you control.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Creatures your opponents control get -1/-0.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nMulticolored creatures you control have deathtouch.', 'Deathtouch\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from a creature you control: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Defender', "Defender\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Nivix Cyclops gets +3/+0 until end of turn and can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.", 'Defender\\n{3}{B}, {T}: Target opponent loses 2 life, then reveals a card at random from their hand.', 'Destroy each nonland permanent with mana value X or less.', "Destroy target artifact or creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Destroy target creature with defender.', "Detain up to two target creatures your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those creatures can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Dimir Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'Double strike\\nSavageborn Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}{R/G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Savageborn Hydra. Activate only as a sorcery.', "Each creature card in your graveyard has scavenge. The scavenge cost is equal to its mana cost. (Exile a creature card from your graveyard and pay its mana cost: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to that card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)\\nSacrifice another creature: Regenerate Varolz, the Scar-Striped.", 'Each opponent loses two times X life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', 'Each player sacrifices a multicolored permanent.', "Enchant creature with power 3 or less\\nWhen Runner's Bane enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.\\n{1}{G}{U}, Return Krasis Incubation to its owner's hand: Put two +1/+1 counters on enchanted creature.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has trample and lifelink. (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks or blocks, its controller loses 2 life.', 'Evolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\nWhenever Renegade Krasis evolves, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Exile all creature cards from target player's graveyard. You gain 3 life for each card exiled this way.", 'Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Put X +1/+1 counters on target creature, where X is the power of the card you exiled.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Extort (Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay {W/B}. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain that much life.)\\nOther creatures you control have extort. (If a creature has multiple instances of extort, each triggers separately.)', "First strike, deathtouch\\nMaster of Cruelties can only attack alone.\\nWhenever Master of Cruelties attacks a player and isn't blocked, that player's life total becomes 1. Master of Cruelties assigns no combat damage this combat.", "First strike, haste\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nEach other creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has haste.", 'First strike\\nRiot Piker attacks each combat if able.', "Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Deputy of Acquittals enters the battlefield, you may return another target creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flash\\nIf an opponent would draw a card except the first one they draw in each of their draw steps, instead that player skips that draw and you draw a card.', "Flash\\nThis spell can't be countered.\\nReach, protection from blue", 'Flying', 'Flying, first strike', 'Flying, vigilance\\nWhenever Jelenn Sphinx attacks, other attacking creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nHexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'Flying\\nMulticolored creatures you control have flying.', "Flying\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Flying\\nWhenever Mirko Vosk, Mind Drinker deals combat damage to a player, that player reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal four land cards, then puts those cards into their graveyard.', "Flying\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, you may switch Fluxcharger's power and toughness until end of turn.", 'Flying\\n{T}: Goblin Test Pilot deals 2 damage to any target chosen at random.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)\\nProtection from green", 'Gain control of target permanent until end of turn. Untap it. It gains haste until end of turn.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Golgari Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Gruul Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Haste', 'Haste\\nMulticolored creatures you control have haste.', 'Haste\\nWhen Viashino Firstblade enters the battlefield, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'If you would draw a card while you have no cards in hand, instead you draw two cards and you lose 1 life.', 'Indestructible\\nBattalion — Whenever Tajic, Blade of the Legion and at least two other creatures attack, Tajic gets +5/+5 until end of turn.', 'Izzet Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nExtort (Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay {W/B}. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain that much life.)', 'Lifelink, protection from white and from black\\nAs long as you have 30 or more life and an opponent has 10 or less life, Blood Baron of Vizkopa gets +6/+6 and has flying.', 'Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal up to two instant and/or sorcery cards from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Maze's End enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Return Maze's End to its owner's hand: Search your library for a Gate card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. If you control ten or more Gates with different names, you win the game.", "Monocolored creatures can't block this turn.", 'Orzhov Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Play with the top card of your library revealed.\\nYou may cast instant and sorcery spells from the top of your library.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell from your library, copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "Populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to creature tokens you control.', "Protection from red\\nWhen Lavinia of the Tenth enters the battlefield, detain each nonland permanent your opponents control with mana value 4 or less. (Until your next turn, those permanents can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Punish the Enemy deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker and 3 damage to target creature.', 'Put three +1/+1 counters on target creature.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Rakdos Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', "Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nScavenge {4}{G}{G} ({4}{G}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Red creatures you control get +1/+0.\\nWhite creatures you control get +0/+1.\\n{R}{W}, Exile Legion's Initiative: Exile all creatures you control. At the beginning of the next combat, return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control and those creatures gain haste until end of turn.", 'Regenerate target creature.', "Return each creature that dealt damage this turn to its owner's hand.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. Morgue Burst deals damage to any target equal to the power of the card returned this way.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)", 'Return target permanent card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Rot Farm Skeleton can't block.\\n{2}{B}{G}, Mill four cards: Return Rot Farm Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery.", 'Sacrifice a creature: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Selesnya Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Simic Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains double strike until end of turn.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target creature gets +2/+4 until end of turn.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target creature gets +5/+5 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Target creature gets -4/-2 until end of turn.', 'Target creature you control gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.\\nOverload {1}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it fights target creature an opponent controls. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', "Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose up to X nonland cards from it and exile them. For each card exiled this way, search that player's graveyard, hand, and library for any number of cards with the same name as that card and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'Target player discards two cards.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target player draws two cards and loses 2 life.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target player mills eight cards.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target player mills two cards. Draw two cards.', 'Trample\\nEvolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)', 'Trample\\nMulticolored creatures you control have trample.', 'Until end of turn, creatures you control gain "When this creature dies, it deals 2 damage to target creature an opponent controls."', 'Until end of turn, target creature loses all abilities and becomes a red Weird with base power and toughness 0/1.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Until end of turn, target creature you control becomes a blue and red Dragon with base power and toughness 4/4, loses all abilities, and gains flying.\\nOverload {3}{U}{U}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Vigilance, protection from creatures\\nWhenever a creature deals combat damage to you, destroy that creature. Create a 1/1 white and black Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Vigilance, reach\\nRuric Thar, the Unbowed attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever a player casts a noncreature spell, Ruric Thar deals 6 damage to that player.', 'Vigilance\\nMulticolored creatures you control have vigilance.', "Warleader's Helix deals 4 damage to any target and you gain 4 life.", "When Deadbridge Chant enters the battlefield, mill ten cards.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, choose a card at random in your graveyard. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put it into your hand.", 'When Opal Lake Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, you may draw a card.', 'When Saruli Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, you gain 7 life.', 'When Scab-Clan Giant enters the battlefield, it fights target creature an opponent controls chosen at random.', "When Scion of Vitu-Ghazi enters the battlefield, if you cast it from your hand, create a 1/1 white Bird creature token with flying, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'When Sin Collector enters the battlefield, target opponent reveals their hand. You choose an instant or sorcery card from it and exile that card.', 'When Smelt-Ward Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, gain control of target creature an opponent controls until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.', 'When Sunspire Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance.', "When Trostani's Summoner enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance, a 3/3 green Centaur creature token, and a 4/4 green Rhino creature token with trample.", 'When Ubul Sar Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, target creature an opponent controls gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Haazda Snare Squad attacks, you may pay {W}. If you do, tap target creature an opponent controls.', "Whenever a creature blocks, that creature's controller loses 1 life.\\n{1}{B}{R}: Regenerate Carnage Gladiator.", 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield this turn, you may draw a card.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Whenever a creature you control attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell from their hand, that player exiles it, then exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile a card that shares a card type with it. That player may cast that card without paying its mana cost. Then they put all cards exiled with Possibility Storm on the bottom of their library in a random order.', 'Whenever a player taps a land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced.', 'Whenever an instant or sorcery spell you control deals damage, create two 1/1 red and white Soldier creature tokens with haste.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell during your turn or when Voice of Resurgence dies, create a green and white Elemental creature token with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control."', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, Bronzebeak Moa gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'You gain 1 life for each creature your opponents control. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to you this turn.', 'You may have Progenitor Mimic enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "At the beginning of your upkeep, if this creature isn\'t a token, create a token that\'s a copy of this creature."', 'You may tap or untap target permanent, then you may tap or untap another target permanent.\\nCipher (Then you may exile this spell card encoded on a creature you control. Whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player, its controller may cast a copy of the encoded card without paying its mana cost.)', '[+1]: Tap target permanent, then untap another target permanent.\\n[−2]: Ral Zarek deals 3 damage to any target.\\n[−7]: Flip five coins. Take an extra turn after this one for each coin that comes up heads.', '{3}: Feral Animist gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is its power.', '{5}{G}: Kraul Warrior gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', '{G}{U}, {T}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target artifact, creature, or land.', '{G}{U}: Beetleform Mage gets +2/+2 and gains flying until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{T}: Add {B} or {G}.\\n{B}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Golgari Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {B} or {R}.\\n{B}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Rakdos Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {G} or {U}.\\n{G}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Simic Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{G}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Selesnya Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nWhenever you tap Zhur-Taa Druid for mana, it deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {R} or {G}.\\n{R}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Gruul Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {R} or {W}.\\n{R}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Boros Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {U} or {B}.\\n{U}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Dimir Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {U} or {R}.\\n{U}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Izzet Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {W} or {B}.\\n{W}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Orzhov Cluestone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {W} or {U}.\\n{W}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Azorius Cluestone: Draw a card.', "{U}: Exile Aetherling. Return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.\\n{U}: Aetherling can't be blocked this turn.\\n{1}: Aetherling gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\n{1}: Aetherling gets -1/+1 until end of turn."]
flavor: ['"All pilots and prototypes destroyed. Extensive collateral damage inflicted. Conclusion: flawless design."\\n—*Manual of Melek*', '"All that steel doesn\'t make them slower. It makes them bolder."\\n—Tajic, Blade of the Legion', '"Break it if you must. The loss of one relic is nothing next to the value of enriching us all."\\n—Suniel the Woodwise', '"Burn. Bleed. Enjoy."\\n—Cluestone inscription', '"Channeling the rage of the beast is the easy part. Explaining why you woke up with no memory in a pile of mangled lawmages—that\'s trickier."', '"Everyone deserves a day in court."', '"Everything serves a purpose. Even you."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Follow your passion, I always say. Might as well get paid to do what you love."', '"I run the maze alone, but I fight with the full might of the Legion."', '"I used to hurl rocks and eat scraps of meat burned over a fire. Look at what I\'ve become and tell me Simic does not hold infinite possibility."', '"I\'m in the field of procurement, and business is good. The guilds want all kinds of maps and relics these days, though what they want them for I\'m not quite sure."', '"In case of fire, treachery, citywide riot, political upheaval, or worldwide societal collapse, break glass."\\n—Cluestone inscription', '"It preys on those who would spy on our lands, so we never prey on it."\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"It\'s always satisfying to stymie the best efforts of a rival, but the reactions of the Gruul are particularly amusing."\\n—Bori Andon, Izzet blastseeker', '"Let him in. He\'s on the list."\\n—Olrich, Rakdos club owner', '"Only the decadent think magic should be pristine and without cost."', '"Ravnicans need order. If they don\'t have it, we shall bring it to them."\\n—Isperia', '"Scores will die in the name of peace. That is what you call compromise?"\\n—Gideon Jura, to Aurelia', '"Sometimes it forgets to loosen its grip before taking flight. I lost my roof that way."\\n—Ecaban, Boros scout', '"That must weigh heavily on your soul. Let me purge it for you."', '"The Obzedat have revived you with purpose. Don\'t squander their blessing."\\n—Teysa Karlov, Grand Envoy of Orzhov', '"The gift of life must be freely given. Anything less would diminish us all."\\n—Arin, Selesnya healer', '"The maaka remain loyal to us in this time of strife. We don\'t even have to feed them—our enemies do."\\n—Nedja, Gruul shaman', '"The maze seems to fight us at every turn, resisting our efforts to solve it."\\n—Niv-Mizzet', '"The most insidious thing in the world is nonsense that sounds just plausible enough to listen to."\\n—Lazav', '"There is no time to remedy our enemies\' ignorance. Blast it out of them."\\n—Aurelia', '"We are all decaying, always in a state of near-death. One moment without breath and we begin to break down."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We are the heart of the wild, the fire in its eyes, and the howl in its throat. Come, join the battle to which you were born."\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"We do not believe in hiding our wealth in the shadows. This is Orzhov, and this is how we reward greatness."\\n—Teysa Karlov, Grand Envoy of Orzhov', '"We have confiscated your spells as evidence. Once we conclude our investigation, you may petition to have them returned."', '"We learned something from the Simic. Unfortunately for them."\\n—Nefara, Dimir agent', '"We raised eelhawks to control the squidflies, then waspcrabs to prey on the eelhawks. Now what do we do with all these waspcrabs?"\\n—Gulistan, Simic biomancer', '"Welcome to my collection."', '"When justice descends, the servant will burn with the master."\\n—Aurelia', '"When the Simic say to take command of your life, we don\'t mean just your career."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Why do guards always look surprised when we bash them?" asked Ruric. "I think they expect a bribe," said Thar.', '"You can always count on the Azorius to ruin a party."\\n—Massacre Girl', '"You caught something on a cold night\'s stroll? No, I\'d say something caught you."\\n—Mezim Magrah, civic healer', '"You see a bird, an oak, a packbeast. I see the potential for an army."\\n—Lalia, Selesnya dryad', '"You will pass with respect, or you will not pass at all."', "A lawmage's runic script is an act of governance given form: legislation written directly onto the air itself.", 'A symbol of power and wealth, the only commodities that matter to the Orzhov.', 'A true Boros commando only calls for reinforcements so they can clean up the mess.', 'Air currents whip through the city corridors, creating wind tunnels that accelerate urban drakes toward their prey.', "As Trostani's influence grew, vitality spread through the Conclave—much to the other guilds' dismay.", 'Beyond lies the culmination of all Izzet projects, a grand experiment led by the dragon Niv-Mizzet himself.', 'Every part of the gate was reclaimed from forgotten ruins and imbued with new purpose by the Swarm.', 'Every soldier returns from battle changed: by hardship, by blood, by a glimpse of glory.', 'Every street corner is a hunting ground, every citizen potential prey.', 'Few among the Azorius have ever spoken with the sphinxes, but all have felt their influence.', 'For the Gruul, bone-crushing rage is the first priority. Accuracy comes in a distant ninetieth.', 'For the Rakdos, "suicidal charge" and "good showmanship" are one and the same.', 'Forgotten under rocks and vines, Gruul symbols mark the sites of primitive rituals where shamans once chanted to the wild.', 'Golgari mold collects whispers, intelligence that is later harvested by Jarad and his high chancellors.', 'Golgari reclaimers resent the gorgons, begrudging the loss of so many fine nutrients locked away in stone.', "He doesn't care whether he's rioting about trade rights or just having a drunken brawl. He wakes up every morning eager to smash some heads.", "In Ravnica's wilder districts, nature still stirs, and its protectors still mind their posts.", 'In the cold corridors of the undercity, misinformation unfurls from Duskmantle like a spreading stain.', 'It holds within it an unsolvable riddle. A creative answer yields an invitation to the guild.', 'It promises protection to those in need and proclaims a warning to any who would threaten Ravnican law.', 'It returned to the leylines as quickly as it had appeared, leaving only broken bodies to mark its passage.', 'It waits in the chill of the undercity, holding nameless secrets for those who dare to touch it.', 'Its three sides represent the Sova, judges and arbitrators; the Jelenn, scribes and elocutors; and the Lyev, lawmages and enforcers.', "Its victims become mindless lunatics. Conveniently, that's the first step in joining the Cult of Rakdos.", 'Leaders shape the minds of their allies. It takes a master to shape the minds of enemies.', 'Make sure you bleed the fine print.', "Many Ravnicans think of nature as orderly groves and elf-tended rot farms. They haven't seen the Gruul wilds.", 'Maze-runners who pass through the Rakdos gate leave behind their scruples and a significant amount of skin.', 'Mirko Vosk hunted anyone with knowledge of the maze, draining the chances of the other guilds.', 'Not the foulest or bloodiest act at Rix Maadi by a stretch.', 'One part mizzium, two parts elemental energy, eleven parts danger.', 'Phytohydras are banned as houseplants in many residential spires. If left unfed, they find their own exit—usually at the cost of extensive property damage.', "Rakdos rioters paint their faces to resemble the drakes' bloodied muzzles.", "Ral Zarek's brainstorms bring actual thunder and lightning.", "Sentries guard Ravnica's landmarks and outlying districts, unaware of these places' import to the maze.", "Simic biomancers don't concern themselves with guarding a gate. Their ever-present creations are enough to ward off trespassers.", 'Simic symbols are among the most intricate and fragile, yet few vandalize them for fear of the strange lifeforms that might be released.', "Some of Orzhov's cruelest collectors remember their debtors by taste alone.", 'Some see the world as a place of infinite wonder and knowledge. Some see it as an infinite dinner plate.', "The Azorius have so many codes and statutes that you're always in violation of one of them.", 'The Azorius symbol stares down like a great eye, reminding visitors of the watchful presence of Isperia and her lawmages.', "The Dimir employ the spirits of Ravnica's ancient, nameless dead, guiding their malevolence toward selected victims.", 'The Golgari maze-runner Varolz hungers to prove his fortitude in battle, and his trail of victims feeds other hungers.', 'The Gruul seek unbounded strength. The Dimir deliver cruel irony.', 'The Implicit Maze winds through Ravnica, connecting arcane landmarks of all ten guilds.', "The Selesnya welcome all to help them heal the city's wounds. The price, however, is devotion to the guild and a selfless belief in Trostani.", "The audience quickly realized a few things: it wasn't a magic trick, there wasn't candy in there, and they'd need new clothes.", "The consciousness of Mat'Selesnya does not always spread in peaceful ways.", 'The devout sacrifice themselves to it hoping for escape from their debts to the guild, but many end up owing in the afterlife.', 'The insectile kraul lurk in the tunnels below street level. Many are loyal to the Golgari Swarm, but others follow their own esoteric caste system.', 'The pattern of the Implicit Maze extends in more than two dimensions.', "The rot farmer's first rite of passage is to craft a pair of work stilts.", 'The route has been known for millennia, but only by those with no means to tell it.', 'The scarred rubble around the gate is testament to past meetings of the Clans, summits that inevitably devolved into brawls.', 'There are many gates into the undercity, but few ways out.', 'They fight for their home with more loyalty than any conscript.', "They've been probation officers, army grunts, bounty hunters—anything to make their district safer.", 'Travelers in the undercity dread the horrors and assassins of the Dimir, but nearly as many die from more mundane hazards.', 'When Selesnya needed a champion, Emmara put the ranks of her guild before herself—making her the perfect choice.', 'When the guilds cooperate, the guildless celebrate their peaceful society. When the guilds clash, the guildless just try to keep out of the way.', 'Wolf-riders of Selesnya apprentice from a young age. Each rider raises a wolf pup from birth to serve as a mount, hoping that one day the two will share the honor of guarding the Great Concourse.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Drew Baker', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Velhagen', 'Eytan Zana', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Ryman', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Maciej Kuciara', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Winters', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Zoltan Boros']
